[?2004l[?2004huser@06993146764c:~/infra-configs$ cat > SECURITY.md << 'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> # Security Issue: Bypassed Pre-commit Hook
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Issue Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> On May 2, 2026, commit 29e769c was pushed by jenkins-bot containing a private key file (`secrets/deploy.key`) with world-readable permissions (0644). This bypassed the pre-commit hook that should have blocked such commits.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Root Cause
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The pre-commit hook was bypassed using the `--no-verify` (or `-n`) flag during commit. This is a common issue with client-side git hooks - they can be easily bypassed by:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Using `git commit --no-verify`
[?2004l[?2004h> - Using `git commit -n`
[?2004l[?2004h> - Disabling hooks in git configuration
[?2004l[?2004h> - Committing from a different repository clone
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Fixes Implemented
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Fixed File Permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - Changed `secrets/deploy.key` from 0644 to 0600
[?2004l[?2004h> - Only the owner can now read/write the file
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Multi-Layer Hook Defense
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Pre-commit Hook** (`.git/hooks/pre-commit`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - First line of defense
[?2004l[?2004h> - Checks staged files for world-readable keys
[?2004l[?2004h> - Can be bypassed with --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Commit-msg Hook** (`.git/hooks/commit-msg`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Second line of defense
[?2004l[?2004h> - Also validates staged files
[?2004l[?2004h> - Runs after pre-commit but can also be bypassed with --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **Pre-push Hook** (`.git/hooks/pre-push`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Third line of defense - MOST IMPORTANT
[?2004l[?2004h> - Validates ALL commits being pushed
[?2004l[?2004h> - Checks historical commits for bad permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - Cannot be bypassed with --no-verify (different flag needed: --no-verify on push)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Catches issues even if commits were made with --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Safe Commit Wrapper
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **safe-commit.sh**
[?2004l[?2004h> - Wrapper script for automation tools (Jenkins, CI/CD, etc.)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Explicitly runs pre-commit hook before committing
[?2004l[?2004h> - Never uses --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> - Ensures hooks are always executed
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Usage for Automation
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For Jenkins/CI/CD Systems
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Instead of:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> git commit -m "auto-update keys"
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Use:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> ./safe-commit.sh -m "auto-update keys"
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### For Manual Commits
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Never use `--no-verify` unless you have a very good reason and have manually verified the changes are safe.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Server-Side Protection (Recommended)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For production environments, implement server-side hooks:
[?2004l[?2004h> - **pre-receive hook** on the Git server
[?2004l[?2004h> - **update hook** on the Git server
[?2004l[?2004h> - These cannot be bypassed by clients
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Testing
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Test that hooks work:
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> # This should be blocked
[?2004l[?2004h> echo "test" > secrets/test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> chmod 644 secrets/test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git add secrets/test.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git commit -m "test"  # Should fail
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> # This should also be blocked at push time even if committed with --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> git commit -m "test" --no-verify  # Commits locally
[?2004l[?2004h> git push  # Should fail due to pre-push hook
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Monitoring
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Review git logs regularly for commits by automation accounts
[?2004l[?2004h> - Audit file permissions in the repository
[?2004l[?2004h> - Consider implementing git commit signing for automation accounts
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## References
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Git Hooks Documentation: https://git-scm.com/docs/githooks
[?2004l[?2004h> - File Permission Best Practices for Private Keys: chmod 600
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
