[?2004huser@06993146764c:~/infra-configs$ cat > HOOKS-README.md << 'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> # Git Hooks Protection System
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This repository uses a multi-layered git hooks system to prevent commits with world-readable private keys (*.pem, *.key files with permissions 0644 or looser).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Active Hooks
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Pre-commit Hook
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `.git/hooks/pre-commit`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Purpose**: First line of defense, checks staged files before commit
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Commit-msg Hook  
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `.git/hooks/commit-msg`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Purpose**: Second line of defense, validates staged files
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git commit --no-verify`
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Pre-push Hook (CRITICAL)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Location**: `.git/hooks/pre-push`
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Purpose**: Validates ALL commits being pushed, even those created with --no-verify
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Advantage**: Catches bad commits before they reach the remote repository
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Limitation**: Can be bypassed with `git push --no-verify`, but this is less common
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## For Automation/CI/CD
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> **IMPORTANT**: Automation tools (Jenkins, CI/CD pipelines) should use the provided wrapper:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> ./safe-commit.sh -m "your commit message"
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This ensures hooks are always executed and cannot be accidentally bypassed.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## What Was Fixed
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - Commit 29e769c contained `secrets/deploy.key` with 0644 permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - This bypassed pre-commit hook (likely used `--no-verify`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Fixed file permissions to 0600
[?2004l[?2004h> - Added pre-push hook to catch future bypasses
[?2004l[?2004h> - Created safe-commit wrapper for automation
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Testing Protection
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> To verify hooks work:
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h> # Create test key with bad permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> echo "test" > secrets/bad.key
[?2004l[?2004h> chmod 644 secrets/bad.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git add secrets/bad.key
[?2004l[?2004h> git commit -m "test"  # Should be BLOCKED
[?2004l[?2004h> ```
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Best Practices
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Never use `--no-verify` unless absolutely necessary
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Always use `chmod 600` for private keys
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Use `./safe-commit.sh` in automation scripts
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Review commits from automation accounts regularly
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Server-Side Protection (Recommended)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> For production, implement server-side hooks on your Git server:
[?2004l[?2004h> - Pre-receive hooks (cannot be bypassed by clients)
[?2004l[?2004h> - Update hooks
[?2004l[?2004h> - Branch protection rules
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> See SECURITY.md for more details.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
